    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0666" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 814.51/210.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 14, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The refusal of the British Government referred to in your telegram of January 12
                    is regarded as tentative. Since a copy of the <pb facs="0667" n="563"
                        xml:id="pg563"/> agreement is at the disposal of the British Foreign Office
                    a favorable reply is hoped for. The Department considers the sending of a
                    special Guatemalan agent to London not to be of any advantage.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
